==English==

===Etymology===
First in use about 1735-40, from {{term|hum||(dialectal and slang) to delude, impose on, cajole}} + {{term|bug||a specter, goblin}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hoax]], [[prank]] or [[jest]]
# A [[fraud]] or [[sham]]
# A [[fraudster]] or [[cheat]]
# {{British}} A type of [[chewy]] [[sweet]] ([[candy]])

